    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0368" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg258"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2336</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Osborne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-19">October 19, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I telegraphed to Lord
                    Reading in the sense of our conversation on Friday evening the 16th and I have
                    now received a reply from him.</p>
                <p>He hopes that his telegram to the Foreign Office, copy of which I enclose<anchor
                        n="84" xml:id="d253-f1"/> for your information, will show you that their
                    chief preoccupation at Geneva has been to do everything possible to fall in with
                    your wishes and as far as possible to remove any difficulties you might have to
                    meet in taking the very important step of allowing an American representative to
                    sit at the Council table. In giving you the above message I am to add that there
                    never was any intention of leaving you to take the sole initiative in invoking
                    the Pact of Paris, that any impression you may have gained to that effect is due
                    to a misunderstanding, and that you can rely on him to maintain the closest
                    possible cooperation with you and with your representative in Geneva.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>D. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
